From 88cf8ea2cfa48043984748f8be24710cdafce9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: netplay <netplay@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:09:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/42] netplay: netplay-server support (rooms + relay, games
 in a RAM folder, catalog)

With server=, room= and key= in netplay.ini, host and join send only to a
netplay-server, which pairs them by room and relays the session packets; only
the server needs an open port. At core load the server's games are fetched
(md5-checked) into a tmpfs, <NES games>/_Netplay server, so the OSD file
browser shows them and nothing is written to the SD card. The server's
catalog of bring-your-own versions gives an OSD warning for another version.

The UDP test also runs through a real server (server/build) that hands out
the game. The harness keeps running briefly after its target so the other
side is not cut off one frame short.
